  "goodToKnow": "Der Grünkohl is kale, a winter staple in northern Germany, cooked for hours with Pinkel or Kohlwurst sausage, Kassler and potatoes. In Bremen and Oldenburg, groups go on a Kohlfahrt, a winter walk with drinking games that ends in a kale feast, where a Kohlkönig is crowned. Tradition says it tastes best after the first frost. Der Kohl is cabbage. It has no plural."
